{"author":{"id":"585844baa6074d44d241f46aa7c9f21ff46653adf617d7f070fbfe327626c989"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794782967,"nonce":"XcBxLyBQJy/TqrzsKSi/xBbG0iY=","message":"Threaded hxcpp through Emscripten in d7d500d (unpushed, on top of e4d0f81). krio-wasm's spawn hook is not needed: with std rebuilt with +atomics,+bulk-memory, Rust's std threads are Emscripten pthreads, so hxn-future's krio_parallel pool and spawn_blocking run on Web Workers (worker_threads under node) as they do natively. hxcpp needs -D HXCPP_MULTI_THREADED_APP on the Haxe command line (its Emscripten toolchain sets HXCPP_SINGLE_THREADED_APP otherwise) and -pthread on every object: the generated @:buildXml extends the emscripten compiler and exe linker under if=\"emscripten hxn_threads\", with -sPTHREAD_POOL_SIZE=8 and -sALLOW_MEMORY_GROWTH=1 (a shared memory cannot grow without it, and the counter ran out at 16 MiB). emrun already sends COOP/COEP.\n\nRun locally (macOS, emsdk 5.0.7, Node 24, Chrome): counter emcc-threads and gen-emcc-threads; examples emcc-threads under node; tests/web node, browser, node-threads, browser-threads (with a new chunks() future whose spawn_blocking threads are started from pool workers); hxn-gpu-webgl2 and hxn-gpu-webgpu checks with cpp --wasm --threads --browser; a threaded package of hxn-gpu-webgl2 compiled through hxn.Bind and run in Chrome. Full suite rerun green: counter all 13 modes, examples hl (Ash), cpp, cppia, emcc, emcc-threads, emcc-page, wasm, wasm-threads, wasm-page, wasm-threads-page, cli hl cpp cppia wasm emcc, cimport emcc and cpp. Not run: Linux, Windows, mobile.\n\nFound: in a web page, examples/downloads deadlocks threaded. Its async fetch resumes on a pool worker and calls spawn_blocking there; Emscripten creates a thread asked for on a worker from the page's thread, which is spinning in await. Under node it passes. So in a web page await still blocks, and now also blocks thread creation from workers; then works. That is why there is no emcc-threads-page example mode.\n\nStill open: -sPROXY_TO_PTHREAD, to run main on a pthread so await works in a web page; that takes the program off the DOM, so the canvas, WebGL2 and WebGPU would go through an OffscreenCanvas (OFFSCREENCANVAS_SUPPORT, or the libraries' own transfer).","files":null}]}